From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:59:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11: write back the scissor rectangle count in
 d3d10_device_RSGetScissorRects.

Given room for the rectangles as well, the Direct3D 10 RSGetScissorRects
left the count it was passed as it was.  Windows returns how many are set,
measured with WARP and the hardware driver: asked for four with one set, it
answers one, and zeroes the rest, as Direct3D 11 does, and as the Direct3D
10 RSGetViewports here already did.  The test added with the last commit
checks the count this way.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit da080934bae9a554b3853fcaabf1e9e1e96c7808)

diff --git a/dlls/d3d11/device.c b/dlls/d3d11/device.c
index b7e2e1d0c9c..5cd58feb318 100644
--- a/dlls/d3d11/device.c
+++ b/dlls/d3d11/device.c
@@ -7056,14 +7056,10 @@ static void STDMETHODCALLTYPE d3d10_device_RSGetScissorRects(ID3D10Device1 *ifac
     wined3d_device_context_get_scissor_rects(device->immediate_context.wined3d_context, &actual_count, rects);
     wined3d_mutex_unlock();
 
-    if (!rects)
-    {
-        *rect_count = actual_count;
-        return;
-    }
-
-    if (*rect_count > actual_count)
+    /* the count comes back as it does from RSGetViewports, when there is room for the rectangles as well */
+    if (rects && *rect_count > actual_count)
         memset(&rects[actual_count], 0, (*rect_count - actual_count) * sizeof(*rects));
+    *rect_count = actual_count;
 }
 
 static HRESULT STDMETHODCALLTYPE d3d10_device_GetDeviceRemovedReason(ID3D10Device1 *iface)
